<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dominador Gómez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1929">1929</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dominador Gómez was a Filipino physician, labour leader and politician who headed the Unión Obrera Democrática, one of the first Filipino labour federations, from 1903. In 1906 he acted as intermediary between the American authorities and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macario-sakay">Macario Sakay</a>, persuading him to surrender on the promise of an amnesty that was not honoured. He was later elected to the Philippine Assembly for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dominador-gomez.jpg" alt="Dominador Gómez" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anthony R. Tuohy, suplemento español del The Far Eastern Review, Manila I.F. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dominador_G%C3%B3mez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
